    "COLOUR TESTING SCHEME (DETAILS): Notwithstanding the approved plans, the development hereby permitted shall not be implemented until a detailed colour testing scheme has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The scheme shall include:\r\n\r\n(a) The criterion for assessing which colour is most suitable, with visual compatibility being one of the key criteria; and\r\n(b) A timeline for the implementation of the colour change, which must be completed within 2 months from the date of approval of the colour testing scheme. \r\n\r\nThe development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved colour scheme and retained and maintained as such thereafter into perpetuity. \r\n\r\nREASON: In order to safeguard the special architectural or historic interest of the heritage asset, to ensure the chosen colour is appropriate for the building and its setting, and to ensure that the colour change is implemented in a timely manner."
